Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - commit Aurora World Fabric stores at shutdown

Folia's shutdown saves every chunk and waits for the region-file I/O
queue to drain, but never calls RegionFileStorage.flush() or close().
Region files do not need it: each write already went to the OS. AWF
does: its writes are in memory until a commit, so without this the
last interval of a listed world's chunks was lost on every stop.

The call sits right after MoonriseRegionFileIO.flush(server), the
point where every chunk save has reached its storage, and before the
chunk system's executors halt. It commits and closes every open AWF
storage on the stopping thread. With no world in aurora.awf.worlds
there is nothing open and it returns at once.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
index b89c0d0a7ab6b4e9e8adf13de734c92c8b81d9c5..a63312e01cc7875423e8850441522cf5a37d74a0 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
@@ -1130,6 +1130,7 @@ public abstract class MinecraftServer extends ReentrantBlockableEventLoop<TickTa
         LOGGER.info("Waiting for all RegionFile I/O tasks to complete...");
         ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.io.MoonriseRegionFileIO.flush((MinecraftServer)(Object)this);
         LOGGER.info("All RegionFile I/O tasks to complete");
+        dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.awf.AwfEngine.closeAll(); // SourbyCraft - Aurora World Fabric: every save has reached its storage
         if ((Object)this instanceof net.minecraft.server.dedicated.DedicatedServer) {
             ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.MoonriseCommon.haltExecutors();
         }
